"Bitcoin mining is bad for the environment" was easily the most pervasive FUD during the 2020 bull run. 

@SGBarbour challenged this narrative by popularizing flare gas mining: using stranded methane from oil production to power ASICs, instead of venting or flaring excess methane into the atmosphere as was previously standard. 

Because methane is a far more potent greenhouse gas than CO₂, converting methane into CO₂ through Bitcoin mining reframed Bitcoin as a potential emissions-reduction tool rather than a simple polluter.

